rkets price Democratic chances at only 5-6%", "Open seat with no incumbent penalty or benefit on either side"], "rationale": "The state's Republican lean, a polling average near R+10 including a fresh October survey, and markets giving Johnson about a 5% chance all point to a comfortable but not absolutely safe Republican hold. Most raters call it Solid or Safe R, though one says Lean R, justifying a Likely R label rather than Safe.", "watch": "A strong debate performance or a late Democratic-leaning national environment could tighten the race, but Johnson would need a substantial shift to contend.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Henry McMaster (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Carolina's open governor's race pits Republican Attorney General Alan Wilson against Democratic state Representative Jermaine Johnson, with incumbent Henry McMaster term-limited. The state's Republican fundamentals give the GOP a clear edge, and recent polling shows Wilson leading by roughly eight to ten points, including an October survey with a 45-35 margin. Prediction markets give Johnson only about a five percent chance of winning.\n\nMost expert raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Republican column, though one rates it Lean R, suggesting some residual uncertainty in an open-seat contest. Johnson has kept the race competitive in tone, with the candidates clashing over affordability, Medicaid, gambling, and abortion during their October debate, but the structural environment favors Wilson. The race remains a likely Republican hold with limited upside for an upset.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0588, "margin": -9.1}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0546, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0722, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0597, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0544, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0532, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0678